ncluding a New York Times/Siena survey giving her a 7-point lead in early October, while Republican-leaning pollsters show a narrower race.\nPeltola has outraised Sullivan substantially, though outside groups have spent heavily against her. Prediction markets give her roughly a 72% chance of winning. Alaska's Republican-leaning electorate and Sullivan's incumbency keep this within reach for the GOP, but the current polling and money picture points to a small Democratic advantage heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5747, "margin": 0.87}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6995, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6035, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5728, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6289, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6246, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.603, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6381, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6392, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6469, "margin": 2.5}]}